From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32, comctl32: create the XP shell's controls from Wine's themed controls

Purpose: draw buttons, edits and combo boxes in XP shell dialogs with the theme.
The XP shell runs the native comctl32 without its SxS activation context,
so its dialogs (Run, Folder Options, property sheets) got user32's classic
Button, ComboBox, Edit, ListBox and Static, where XP shows themed v6
controls. In such a process of the opted-in external shell, user32 now
creates those classes from Wine's themed implementations in the separately
named controls module, as already done for the Start button. The classes
are registered as "win4wine!" + name with the prefix as their version, so
GetClassName still reports Button, Edit and so on to the native code. This
replaces the ComboBoxEx-only alias of the address bar; its XP measurements
still hold (tests/toolbar-layout.c reports XP's layout and the drop-down
button's pixels equal XP's). Processes with Wine's own comctl32 are not
affected.

